## Common Pitfalls

### Zustand Selector Infinite Loop
Selector returns new array/object every render → always memoize filters with `useMemo`.

### CSS Specificity Conflicts
Avoid dynamic Tailwind classes; use static classes or `style` attribute.

### S3 Host Header
Custom HTTP handler must skip `host` header — otherwise signature mismatch. Already handled in `s3Client.ts`.

### HTML5 Drag & Drop
Do NOT use `onDragStart`/`onDrop` — unreliable in Tauri WebView2. Use the existing mouse-based system in `FileList.tsx`.

### Folder Operations (B2-safe)
- Folders are virtual in S3 (prefix ending in `/`)
- `ListObjectsV2` with `Delimiter: "/"` → `CommonPrefixes` = folders, `Contents` = files
- Rename/delete folders: must recursively copy/move all children first
- R2/B2 don't support `ListBuckets` — use `defaultBucket` field in connection

## Before Committing
```bash
pnpm tsc --noEmit && pnpm vite build
```

## Push Workflow
When asked to push:
1. Check commits: `git log v{last}..HEAD --oneline`
2. Determine version (fix=patch, feat=minor, feat!/BREAKING=major)
3. Update CHANGELOG.md with new version section (Added/Changed/Fixed/UI/Performance)
4. Commit changelog: `git commit -m "docs: update changelog for v{x.x.x}"`
5. Create tag: `git tag -a v{x.x.x} -m "Release description"`
6. Push: `git push origin main --tags`

## Known Issues / Technical Debt
- `AddConnectionModal.tsx` is legacy (superseded by `ConnectionFormPage.tsx`)
- `download_file` Rust command is TODO — large files still via JS
- Download cancellation not functional
- Credentials stored plaintext in localStorage (no OS keychain)
- `greet` command in Rust backend is dead code
- `FileList.tsx` is ~2300 lines — candidate for refactoring
- CSP disabled (`"csp": null`)
